        {
          "id": 1720705289,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> Looks good to me, but do we need similar handling of STTYPE_UNPARSED in the other `check_relation_*()` functions as well?\n\n* [x] check_relation_LHS_FIELD\n* [x] check_relation_LHS_FVALUE\n* [x] check_relation_LHS_SLICE\n* [x] check_relation_LHS_FUNCTION\n* [x] check_relation_LHS_ARITHMETIC\n\nI did however had to rework the implementation, because just relying on `check_arithmetic()` to \"do the right thing\", i.e., call `resolve_unparsed()` and assume that `FAIL`s is not right. Calling it ourselves, and asserting it to `FAIL` is better, IMHO.\n\n> It would also be good to have a test case in test/suite_dfilter/ somewhere.\n\nYes, I've cleaned up the test code I used and added that here too.",
          "author": {
